{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>Once by my holy [ones]</b> — the heavens, for they stand perpetually: 'for I lift my hands to the heavens' [Deuteronomy 32:40]. Or 'by my holy [ones]' there, like 'my holiness' [i.e., the verse means 'by my holiness']. The sense of 'once' is that it is sufficient, or that I have never sworn by my holiness, except this oath alone is the trustworthy one — that his seed shall not cease forever. Therefore: 'his seed and his throne like the sun before me' — in the days of the Messiah."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 89, :notes {0 "The Hebrew is compressed and elliptical throughout; rendered hyper-literally without smoothing."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:37.552732548Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}